title: "Prep-work and Setup for the 'Cloud-Native Architectures and Modern Data Formats for Geoscience' course"
message: >-
  Please cite this lesson using the metadata from this file when referring to
  or reusing this training material.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Tobias
    family-names: Ferreira
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0888-9751"
    affiliation: "National Oceanography Centre"
abstract: >-
  A Carpentries-style prep-work and setup lesson for the course
  "Cloud-Native Architectures and Modern Data Formats for Geoscience". The
  prep-work covers essential foundations in shell usage, introductory xarray
  workflows with a NetCDF sea surface temperature example, and Git/GitHub
  collaboration basics, together with setup guidance before the main course.
